{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f37e39d99b57bc5b31", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Classification of Elements and Periodicity in Properties - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f19c"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f199", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f132", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b41"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : The metallic radius of \\(\\mathrm{Na}\\) is \\(1.86 \\mathrm{~A}^{\\circ}\\) and the ionic radius of \\(\\mathrm{Na}^{+}\\)is lesser than \\(1.86 \\mathrm{~A}^{\\circ}\\).\nStatement II : Ions are always smaller in size than the corresponding elements.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "e24970", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f133"}, {"id": "9165ce", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f134"}, {"id": "b4c72a", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f135"}, {"id": "599bfa", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f136"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f137", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52dc"], "question": {"text": "The first ionization enthalpies of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> follow the order"}, "options": [{"id": "15568d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f138"}, {"id": "dc4261", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Be</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f139"}, {"id": "920002", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13a"}, {"id": "13b191", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b41"], "question": {"text": "The correct orders among the following are<br />Atomic radius : $\\mathrm{B} \\lt \\mathrm{Al} \\lt \\mathrm{Ga} \\lt \\mathrm{In} \\lt \\mathrm{Tl}$<br />Electronegativity : $\\mathrm{Al} \\lt \\mathrm{Ga} \\lt \\mathrm{In} \\lt \\mathrm{Tl} \\lt \\mathrm{B}$<br />Density : $\\mathrm{Tl} \\lt \\mathrm{In} \\lt \\mathrm{Ga} \\lt \\mathrm{Al} \\lt \\mathrm{B}$<br />1st Ionisation Energy : In $ \\lt \\mathrm{Al} \\lt \\mathrm{Ga} \\lt \\mathrm{Tl} \\lt \\mathrm{B}$<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "2186fc", "text": "B and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13d"}, {"id": "ef6807", "text": "A and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13e"}, {"id": "43541c", "text": "C and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f13f"}, {"id": "dc8d11", "text": "A and B Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f140"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f141", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52dc"], "question": {"text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> has a smaller first ionization enthalpy than <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math>. Consider the following statement:<br />(I) it is easier to remove <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> electron than<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp; electron<br />(II) <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> electron of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is more shielded from the nucleus by the inner core of electrons than the <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> electrons of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math><br />(III) <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> electron has more penetration power than <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></math> electron<br />(IV) atomic radius of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is more than <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math><br />(atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> )<br />The correct statements are."}, "options": [{"id": "71ef98", "text": "(I), (II) and (IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f142"}, {"id": "dd6de5", "text": "(II), (III) and (IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f143"}, {"id": "002adb", "text": "(I), (II) and (III)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f144"}, {"id": "7b1b11", "text": "(I), (III) and (IV)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f145"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f146", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b41"], "question": {"text": "The ionic radii of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> are in the order :"}, "options": [{"id": "cdc93b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f147"}, {"id": "c297a3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f148"}, {"id": "d7a953", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f149"}, {"id": "cee989", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Al</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52dc"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I:</strong> The decrease in first ionization enthalpy from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math> is much larger than that from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Al</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math>.</p><p><strong>Statement II:</strong> The d orbitals in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ga</mi></math> are completely filled.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fc6ae0", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14c"}, {"id": "758e61", "text": "Both the statements I and II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14d"}, {"id": "a7e838", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14e"}, {"id": "cf8148", "text": "Both the statements I and II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f14f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f150", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d3035eaf049203d85366a4"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b41"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : In group 13, the stability of +1 oxidation state increases down the group. Statement II : The atomic size of gallium is greater than that of aluminium. In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "5997ac", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f151"}, {"id": "11b05d", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f592ee0e063d926f152"}, {"id": "09efa5", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": nu